WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.390
0-100 km/h
is the standard test

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.370
for how fast a car accelerates.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.560
The Brits call it
"nought to sixty" mph.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.690
An everyday road car
with a bit of power

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.850
can do that in
six or seven seconds.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.430
A Formula One car, about two seconds.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.262
As I record this, the fastest-accelerating
road-legal car in the world

00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:20.460
is the Rimac Nevera,
which can go

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.460
from 0 to 100km/h
in 1.85 seconds.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.460
This is "mythen", built by a team
from ETH Zurich, a Swiss university,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.810
and it hits 100km/h
in under a second.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.950
- This car is the current holder
of the world record in acceleration

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.520
from 0-100km/h
for electric vehicles.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.760
For the world record project,
we brought together a team

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.800
of alumni and current team members,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.930
some are students,
some are recent graduates.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.680
We took a car that was fully designed
by students, we modified it.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.800
That also allowed some of the members
that are still students

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.228
to do research and make a master thesis.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.863
- And I'm about to get in it and do that.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:16.342
But there is quite a history of
floppy-haired British presenters

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.020
getting into high-speed vehicles
and ending up in hospital,

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.500
so I've got a lot of safety
briefing to do first.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.480
- To build a car that can go
this fast, you really need

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.490
to go down to the first
principles of physics.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.190
You need to be able to put
enough force into the ground

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.840
in a very short amount of time.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.120
Just pure grip reaches its limits

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.190
at around 1½ seconds, approximately.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.920
To get more force into the ground,
we use a self-developed system,

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.480
which we call "power ground effect".

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.600
We suck the air out underneath the car
from a big plate,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.220
and this pulls the car to the ground

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.320
to make the car accelerate faster.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.470
We use two fans that power up
shortly before launch

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.640
to pull the car down,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.380
to be able to create
that under-pressure.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.540
However, for the back wheels,
we need more torque.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.450
So for this, we developed
a new generation of motors

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.540
that has approximately
twice the amount of torque.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.900
Each of the motors has
approximately the same power

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.700
as a small hatchback.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.480
- Everything is custom, self-designed,
so it's quite expensive.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.320
The main source of parts is from
our sponsors from the industry.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.500
We also get a lot of
support from the university.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.520
Our mission is not to build race cars,
it is to build up engineers.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.900
- At world record pace,

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.100
a lightweight driver in here
pulls 3.8 Gs peak acceleration.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.840
I'm going to add about
30 more kilos of weight,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.020
so I'm not going to quite hit that pace,
but it's going to be close.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.030
It's almost as fast as the catapult

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.370
that launches fighter jets
from aircraft carriers.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.860
It's faster than any rollercoaster launch

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.440
apart from one in Japan
that's currently closed

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.260
because it kept shattering people's bones.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.410
There are cars which take
off faster than "mythen" here,

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.260
but they're top fuel dragsters
running on nitromethane,

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.090
loud enough to cause hearing damage,

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:53.070
and not suitable for anything other

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.380
than going in
a straight line for a few seconds.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.770
And yes, I will just be going in
a straight line for a few seconds

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.280
but in theory, I could go
round an actual racetrack.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.310
- Electrically, the main danger
is high voltage.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.380
There are emergency buttons.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.450
Push that button to turn off the car.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.780
If there is, for example,
a fire in the car,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.750
the driver has to be
able to get out quickly.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:19.561
It's something we have to train
just to be quick enough.

00:03:19.561 --> 00:03:21.390
- That was 6.6.
- [sighs]

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.260
- You have to be able to exit
the car within five seconds.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.453
- Go.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.020
- Clear!

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.316
- 4.6.
- That'll do.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.990
- It's absolutely difficult to describe
because it's only a second.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.840
It's a really surreal experience

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.450
because you don't really
believe it just happened.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.510
You go into acceleration mode,
roll to the start,

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.430
initiate power ground effect,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.840
which will suck you to the floor.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.840
- PG, active.

00:03:51.513 --> 00:03:53.483
- Both fans active.
- Yeah.

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:56.341
- Oh boy. Okay.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.720
- You will have to pull on the buttons

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.840
behind the steering wheel
and then push throttle.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.160
And then when you release

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.050
there is a split second
where nothing happens

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.390
but then you will get launched.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.433
- Flaps. Throttle.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.488
[shouts]

00:04:15.995 --> 00:04:16.828
Holy...!

00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:24.319
What!

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:26.970
- After you have reached a hundred kmh,

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.870
the car will shut down.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.878
- What?
- And then you can slowly go on the brakes.

00:04:31.692 --> 00:04:33.277
- What?

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:53.370
That was the longest second
of my life. I...

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.860
Was that really only like
one and a bit seconds?

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.720
That felt like five.
- That was faster.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.610
- That felt like five seconds.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.410
- Pretty much dead on 1.4 seconds.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.290
- 1.4? I mean, it's your
round of applause folks.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.553
Congratulations. That's a heck of a thing.

